Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Stop signing in on the VM console at boot. With autologon on, every boot starts a
; console session, and the first RDP/RemoteApp connect has to take it over ("Please
; wait for ... to respond", ~35 s). Off, the first connect simply starts the session.
; Also removes the plaintext autologon password Windows keeps for it.
; Side effect: the web console (127.0.0.1:8006) shows the sign-in screen.
; Revert: AutoAdminLogon "1" and set DefaultPassword again.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Winlogon]
"AutoAdminLogon"="0"
"DefaultPassword"=-

